IMPORT prelude

-- Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore Act 1992 (Singapore) -- Scheduled public schemes: recovery of wrongly given grants
-- (ss 17A-17E), the false-information offences and their penalties (s 17F), notices, arrest and seized items (ss 17G, 17H, 17I,
-- 17N), composition (s 28A); and the general provisions with decision content: protection from liability (ss 10, 25), secrecy
-- (s 27), the Authority's symbol (s 28), and membership and quorum (s 5, First Schedule paras 7, 9, 11).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/IRASA1992.txt. The revised
-- edition incorporates amendments up to 1 December 2021; later amendments are annotated, the latest seen being S 589/2026 (wef
-- 11 September 2026), which added item 12 (SME Cash Grant 2026) to the Second Schedule. Part 5A was inserted by Act 11 of 2024
-- (wef 1 November 2024).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 8 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the provisions with decision content
-- for an ordinary person or business, which are almost all in Part 5A. Not encoded: incorporation, functions and powers (ss 3-8),
-- staff (s 9), finance (ss 12-17), the 1992 transfer provisions (ss 18-24), entry and search powers in detail (s 17H(1)-(6)),
-- restraint (s 17J), protection of informers (s 27A), service and electronic service (ss 28B, 29), regulations (s 31), and the
-- Third and Fourth Schedules beyond their names. The "prescribed rate" of interest (s 17D) is left to regulations, not retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example rows. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore Act 1992 -- Scheduled public schemes`

-- s 2: "Scheduled public scheme" means a scheme, introduced by the Government or a statutory body, under which "any money, credit,
-- rebate or other grant is to be given, and that is specified in the Second Schedule". Second Schedule items 1-12 (selected here),
-- amendable by the Minister by order in the Gazette (s 30).
DECLARE Scheme IS ONE OF
    `the wage credit scheme`
    `the Jobs Support Scheme`
    `the SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit`
    `the Jobs Growth Incentive`
    `the Rental Support Scheme`
    `the Progressive Wage Credit Scheme`
    `the Uplifting Employment Credit`
    `the SME Cash Grant 2026`
    `a government grant not in the Second Schedule`

GIVEN `the scheme` IS A Scheme
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the scheme is a Scheduled public scheme` IF
    CONSIDER `the scheme`
    WHEN `a government grant not in the Second Schedule` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `17A-17E -- recovery of wrongly given grants`

-- s 17A: applies when a recipient "has been given any amount of money, credit, rebate or other grant under a Scheduled public
-- scheme ... whether before, on or after" the 2024 commencement, "to which the recipient is not entitled under the terms of the
-- Scheduled public scheme". s 17B: the Authority may recover an equal amount "as a debt due to the Government".
GIVEN `the scheme` IS A Scheme, `the recipient was entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may recover the grant as a debt` IF
    `the scheme is a Scheduled public scheme` `the scheme` AND (NOT `the recipient was entitled`)

-- s 17C: written notice to pay "within 30 days after the date of service of the notice or any later time that the Authority may
-- allow in a particular case" (the payment period). Here `days allowed` is the period the Authority allows, 0 if none.
GIVEN `days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the payment period in days` MEANS
    IF `days allowed` GREATER THAN 30 THEN `days allowed` ELSE 30

-- s 17D: if any part is unpaid within the payment period, interest "at the prescribed rate ... calculated on a daily basis from
-- the end of the payment period to the date the claim amount is paid ... in full". s 17E: the Authority may remit or refund the
-- whole or any part of the claim amount or interest. The rate is prescribed elsewhere and not encoded; only the days are.
GIVEN `days allowed` IS A NUMBER, `day paid in full after service` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days of interest` MEANS
    IF `day paid in full after service` GREATER THAN `the payment period in days` `days allowed`
    THEN `day paid in full after service` MINUS `the payment period in days` `days allowed`
    ELSE 0

§§ `17F -- giving false or misleading information`

-- s 17F(1), (3), (5): for the purposes of obtaining, or assisting another to obtain, a grant under a Scheduled public scheme, giving
-- "to a public agency any information that is false or misleading in any material particular" or omitting "any material particular"
-- from a document given to a public agency. Three tiers by fault:
--   (1) no fault element stated -- penalty "equal to the amount" (s 17F(2)); no fine or imprisonment is stated;
--   (3) "without reasonable excuse or through negligence" -- penalty "double the amount", and a fine up to $5,000 or up to 3 years
--       or both (s 17F(4));
--   (5) "wilfully with intent" -- penalty "3 times the amount", and a fine up to $10,000 or up to 3 years or both (s 17F(6)).
-- The amount is the grant given, or that "would have been given ... had the offence not been detected", to which X is not entitled.
DECLARE Fault IS ONE OF
    `no fault shown`
    `without reasonable excuse or through negligence`
    `wilfully with intent`

-- s 17F(7): "public agency" means an Organ of State or a ministry or department of the Government; a public officer; a public
-- authority established by or under any public Act for a public purpose "(other than a Town Council)"; or a member, officer,
-- employee or department of such a public authority.
DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `a ministry`
    `a public officer`
    `a statutory board`
    `an officer of a statutory board`
    `a Town Council`
    `a private company`

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recipient is a public agency` IF
    CONSIDER `the recipient`
    WHEN `a Town Council` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a private company` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the scheme` IS A Scheme, `the recipient` IS A Recipient, `false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `omitted a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 17F offence is made out` IF
        `the scheme is a Scheduled public scheme` `the scheme`
    AND `the recipient is a public agency` `the recipient`
    AND (`false or misleading in a material particular` OR `omitted a material particular`)

GIVEN `the fault` IS A Fault
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the penalty multiple` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the fault`
    WHEN `no fault shown` THEN 1
    WHEN `without reasonable excuse or through negligence` THEN 2
    WHEN `wilfully with intent` THEN 3

GIVEN `the fault` IS A Fault, `the amount not entitled to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 17F penalty` MEANS
    `the penalty multiple` `the fault` TIMES `the amount not entitled to`

GIVEN `the fault` IS A Fault
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 17F maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the fault`
    WHEN `no fault shown` THEN 0
    WHEN `without reasonable excuse or through negligence` THEN 5000
    WHEN `wilfully with intent` THEN 10000

GIVEN `the fault` IS A Fault
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 17F maximum imprisonment in years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the fault`
    WHEN `no fault shown` THEN 0
    WHEN `without reasonable excuse or through negligence` THEN 3
    WHEN `wilfully with intent` THEN 3

§§ `17G, 17H -- notices and investigation`

-- s 17G(2) and s 17H(13): contravening a notice or requirement "without reasonable excuse" -- a fine up to $10,000 or up to 12 months
-- or both, and "in the case of a continuing offence, ... a further fine not exceeding $100 for every day or part of a day during
-- which the offence continues after conviction".
GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for ignoring a notice` MEANS
    10000 PLUS (100 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`)

-- s 17H(9): the time for compliance with a written notice under (8) "is 21 days after the date of service of the notice or any other
-- period that the chief executive officer or authorised investigating officer considers appropriate". Here 0 means no other period.
GIVEN `other period set` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days to comply with a section 17H notice` MEANS
    IF `other period set` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `other period set` ELSE 21

-- s 17H(7): a person need not disclose information covered by "any statutory obligation (other than sections 128, 128A, 129 and 131
-- of the Evidence Act 1893) to observe secrecy" or "information subject to legal privilege". s 17H(16): otherwise "it is not a
-- defence ... that the person is under a duty of secrecy" (a displaced duty of secrecy); s 17H(17), (18): good-faith compliance is
-- not a breach and attracts no civil or criminal action.
DECLARE Secrecy IS ONE OF
    `legal privilege`
    `another statutory secrecy obligation`
    `an Evidence Act sections 128 to 131 obligation`
    `a contractual duty of confidence`

GIVEN `the duty` IS A Secrecy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may withhold the information` IF
    CONSIDER `the duty`
    WHEN `legal privilege` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another statutory secrecy obligation` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `17I, 17N -- arrest, detention and seized items`

-- s 17I(1): the chief executive officer or a specially authorised officer may arrest without warrant a person reasonably believed
-- (a) to have committed "any offence under section 17F(5)", or (b) to be destroying or deleting evidence, or resisting its taking,
-- to hinder or obstruct the exercise of powers.
GIVEN `the fault` IS A Fault, `obstructing by destroying, deleting or resisting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `arrest without warrant is available` IF
    CONSIDER `the fault`
    WHEN `wilfully with intent` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `obstructing by destroying, deleting or resisting`

-- s 17I(5), (6): detention no longer than reasonable, and "must not exceed 48 hours, excluding the time necessary for the journey
-- from the place of arrest to the Magistrate's Court".
GIVEN `hours held before the Magistrate` IS A NUMBER, `journey hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the detention is within the 48-hour limit` IF
    `hours held before the Magistrate` MINUS `journey hours` AT MOST 48

-- s 17N(2): notice to the owner to take custody of a seized item within a period "which must be at least 5 days after the date of
-- service". s 17N(3): if the owner fails or cannot be found, a document (other than discs, tapes and films, paras (d), (e) of the
-- definition) may be disposed of as the chief executive officer directs; anything else must be reported to a Magistrate.
GIVEN `days given in the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the custody notice period is long enough` IF
    `days given in the notice` AT LEAST 5

DECLARE Item IS ONE OF
    `a paper document`
    `a disc or tape`
    `a laptop`

GIVEN `the item` IS A Item
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the chief executive officer may dispose of the unclaimed item` IF
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `a paper document` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `28A -- composition`

-- s 28A(1): a compoundable Part 5A offence may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of" (a) "one half of the amount of
-- the maximum fine prescribed and penalty payable (if any) for that offence"; (b) $10,000. Reading (a) as half of fine plus penalty
-- is an inference from the words "fine prescribed and penalty payable".
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `x` LESS THAN `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER, `penalty payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the lower of` ((`maximum fine` PLUS `penalty payable`) DIVIDED BY 2) 10000

§ `General provisions`

§§ `10, 25 -- protection from proceedings`

-- s 10: no suit lies "personally against any member, officer or employee of the Authority or other person acting under the direction
-- of the Authority for anything which is in good faith done". s 25: "No action or legal proceedings shall be brought against the
-- Authority in respect of any matter relating to any tax for which the Authority is acting as agent of the Government."
GIVEN `acted in good faith in executing the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an officer may be sued personally` IF
    NOT `acted in good faith in executing the Act`

GIVEN `the matter relates to a tax the Authority collects as agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may be sued` IF
    NOT `the matter relates to a tax the Authority collects as agent`

§§ `27, 28 -- secrecy and the Authority's symbol`

-- s 27(1): a present or former member, officer, employee or agent of the Authority, or committee member, must not disclose
-- information about the affairs of the Authority or any other person obtained in performing duties, "Except for the purpose of the
-- performance of his or her duties ... or when lawfully required to do so by any court or where required or allowed by the provisions
-- of any written law". (2): a fine up to $2,000 or up to one year or both.
GIVEN `disclosed information obtained in duties` IS A BOOLEAN, `for duties` IS A BOOLEAN, `required by a court` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `required or allowed by written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is a secrecy offence` IF
        `disclosed information obtained in duties`
    AND (NOT `for duties`)
    AND (NOT `required by a court`)
    AND (NOT `required or allowed by written law`)

-- s 28(2): using a symbol "identical with that of the Authority, or which so resembles" it "as to deceive or cause confusion, or to
-- be likely to" -- a fine up to $2,000 or up to 6 months or both.
GIVEN `identical symbol` IS A BOOLEAN, `likely to deceive or confuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the symbol use is an offence` IF
    `identical symbol` OR `likely to deceive or confuse`

§§ `5 and First Schedule -- membership and meetings`

-- s 5(1): a Chairperson and "not less than 5 and not more than 10 other members as the Minister may determine".
GIVEN `other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority is properly constituted` IF
    `other members` AT LEAST 5 AND `other members` AT MOST 10

-- First Schedule para 9: a person must not be appointed or continue as a member if (a) "an undischarged bankrupt or has made any
-- arrangement with his or her creditors"; or (b) "sentenced to imprisonment for a term of not less than 6 months and has not
-- received a free pardon". Para 7: office vacated on absence without leave "from 3 consecutive meetings".
GIVEN `undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN, `arrangement with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN, `months of imprisonment sentenced` IS A NUMBER,
      `free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is disqualified from membership` IF
        `undischarged bankrupt`
    OR  `arrangement with creditors`
    OR  (`months of imprisonment sentenced` AT LEAST 6 AND (NOT `free pardon`))

GIVEN `consecutive meetings missed without leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member's office is vacated for absence` IF
    `consecutive meetings missed without leave` AT LEAST 3

-- First Schedule para 11(2): "At every meeting of the Authority, 5 members form a quorum."
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meeting is quorate` IF
    `members present` AT LEAST 5
